      "math_academy_id": "q-89748",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{144}, & 0\\le x\\le 12 \\\\ 1, & x>12,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(4<X\\le 6).$",
      "worked_solution": "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X\\le 6) & =P(X\\le 6)-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}}{144}-\\frac{{4}^{2}}{144} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
